WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.930
Hi! Apple, pear, carrot: which isn't a fruit? And how do we guess a word we don't know? Today we'll sort words into groups and guess meanings from context.

2
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.410
Fruit: apple, pear, mango.

3
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.058
Animals: cow, duck, goat.

4
00:00:20.208 --> 00:00:23.538
Body parts: hand, knee, nose.

5
00:00:23.688 --> 00:00:29.970
Odd one out: in apple, pear and carrot, the carrot is a vegetable.

6
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.050
When you meet a new word, read the whole sentence first.

7
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.778
Look for clues around it: the soup was so hot that I blew on it.

8
00:00:38.928 --> 00:00:43.098
Put your guess back into the sentence and see if it makes sense.

9
00:00:43.248 --> 00:00:51.594
Some words have several meanings, so the sentence decides: a bat can be an animal or something we hit a ball with.

10
00:00:51.744 --> 00:00:57.642
Watch out! A bird can fly, but it's still an animal, so it isn't the odd one!

11
00:00:57.792 --> 00:01:02.850
Name the group first: dog, cat and bird are all animals.

12
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:08.010
An apple is a fruit, so apple is the odd one out.

13
00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:17.850
Your turn! Red, blue, chair, green: which is the odd one out? Pause and think.

14
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:24.066
The others are colours; a chair is furniture. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:33.978
Another one! Bus, train, car, bed: which is the odd one out? Pause and think.

16
00:01:34.128 --> 00:01:40.314
The others are transport; a bed is not. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:40.464 --> 00:01:48.522
Here's another! Which one is a body part? Pause and think.

18
00:01:48.672 --> 00:01:53.802
A knee is part of the body. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:53.952 --> 00:02:04.794
Try one more! The glass fell and broke into many pieces. What does pieces mean? Pause and think.

20
00:02:04.944 --> 00:02:12.354
Broken into many small bits: pieces means small parts. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:12.504 --> 00:02:22.722
Try one more! Sam was exhausted after running. What does exhausted mean? Pause and think.

22
00:02:22.872 --> 00:02:28.410
After running he was very tired. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:37.770
Try one more! Mango, banana and which other word go together? Pause and think.

24
00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:44.034
They're all fruit, and papaya is a fruit. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:44.184 --> 00:02:54.426
Last one! The baby giggled when Dad tickled her. What does giggled mean? Pause and think.

26
00:02:54.576 --> 00:03:01.338
Being tickled makes you laugh, so giggled means laughed. Did you get it right?

27
00:03:01.488 --> 00:03:09.762
Remember: to sort words, name the group first. To guess a meaning, read the whole sentence, find clues and check your guess.

28
00:03:09.912 --> 00:03:14.850
When you read a story, try guessing a new word's meaning!

